title: '[frame-benchmarking] Refactor pallet benchmarking backend'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Refactors the FRAME benchmarking infrastructure without changing observable behavior:
      - Deduplicates the per-`BenchmarkSelector` value extraction in `analysis.rs` behind a single
        `get_value` helper and tidies the related call sites.
      - Adds a `BenchmarkBatch::split` convenience method and improves the documentation of
        `BenchmarkBatchSplitResults` and the `Recording`/`BenchmarkRecording` traits.
      - Emits a warning from the benchmarking CLI when a `#[pov_mode]` attribute targets a storage
        item that was never accessed during the benchmark, so stale or misspelled attributes are
        surfaced instead of being silently ignored.
      - Documents the v1 benchmarking macros as soft-deprecated in favor of `v2`. This is a
        documentation-only deprecation; no `#[deprecated]` attribute is added, so existing v1
        benchmarks continue to compile without warnings.

crates:
  - name: frame-benchmarking
    bump: minor
  - name: frame-benchmarking-cli
    bump: patch
